\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record from 1951 to 2025 on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids shows November to December came in under 90% of normal in 37 of 75 years. In 2025 that pair landed at 45% of normal on the middle, while August to September hit 150%. So far in 2026, March to April came in at just 30% on the county&rsquo;s middle value. October to November is the driest pair, with a normal of 5.98 inches.</p>"}
